#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
xsync: small rsync wrapper for local-to-remote project sync.
Reads .xsync.toml from the project root (current dir or any parent).

The remote is normally an SSH target, "host:/path/to/project/", where host is
an alias from ~/.ssh/config (key auth, ideally with ControlMaster so repeated
syncs reuse one connection). A local path (e.g. a mounted volume) also works.

Usage:
    xsync                      # open the session in a terminal
    xsync --verbose            # open the session showing rsync's raw output
    xsync --init               # create a starter .xsync.toml in current dir
    xsync --version            # show the version
    xsync --help               # show this help

Everything else happens on single keys inside the session:
    s  sync the whole project          r  check the connection, send what was queued
    w  watch mode on/off               i  info: the resolved setup
    c  compare, changing nothing       e  list recorded warnings and errors
    f  sync one file or folder         v  verbose on/off (rsync's raw output)
    h  help                            q  quit
"""

